This patch is needed for the Solaris wrapper build of `v8-solaris`.

What it does:
- lets the build reuse a checked-in `src_binding.rs` when
  `RUSTY_V8_SRC_BINDING_PATH` is set
- avoids rebuilding bindings during every local build

Why it is needed:
- the standalone Solaris wrapper installs `librusty_v8.a` together with a known
  good generated binding and wants downstream codex builds to reuse it

--- a/v8-146.4.0/build.rs
+++ b/v8-146.4.0/build.rs
@@ -106,7 +106,11 @@
     }
 
     build_v8(is_asan);
-    build_binding();
+    if env::var("RUSTY_V8_SRC_BINDING_PATH").is_ok() {
+      print_prebuilt_src_binding_path();
+    } else {
+      build_binding();
+    }
 
     return;
   }
